  "final_answer_preview": "Section 22 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, provides that no act is considered an offence if it is committed by a person who, at the time of the act, is unable to comprehend the nature of their actions due to unsoundness of mind. This includes situations where the individual does not realize that their actions are wrong or contrary to the law. Additionally, it mentions that similar considerations apply to acts performed under involuntary intoxication.",
